# unfops.cf -- t_mds.c coverage: unf (unfolding of rank data,
# documented in tda.hlp). Values are per-case preference rankings
# for 3 alternatives (X1,X2,X3); the command finds the permutation
# of alternatives that best aligns all cases' rankings via Kendall's
# tau, and with df= set, writes per-case alignment records.
#
# PROVEN BUG, FIXED: unf1() (called whenever df= is set) had a
# leftover debug exit(0) right after its first-iteration debug
# print (`tda_out("vor unf2\n"); ...; exit(0);`), killing the whole
# process before writing anything and before returning to the rest
# of the command file -- silent truncation, the same failure class
# as the dmet1/ivreg2(opt=3) bugs fixed earlier in this project.
# Confirmed directly: before the fix, the run died after one line of
# debug output with no completion trailer at all; after, it
# correctly reports "Best permutation", writes all 3 records, and
# exits normally. Fixed in both src/t_mds.c and tdaR/src/t_mds.c;
# see README.md's Proven-bug-fixes section.

silent = -1;

nvar(dfile=unfdat.dat, X1=c1, X2=c2, X3=c3);
unf(df=unfout.txt) = X1,X2,X3;
